# DATA CLEANING

Drop irrelevant column(s)

df = df.drop(columns=[“Colour”])

Missing data

df = df.dropna(subset=[“Height”]) drop na not available

Drops all rows where there are no values in the Height column

Replace rows 

df = df.fillna({“Height”: “None”})

This has replaced any values in the Height column that are missing with “None”

Replace data with other data

df[“Colour”] = df[“Colour”].replace({“Red”: “Blue”})

Standardise text 

df[“Name”] = df[“Name”].str.lower() - changes all the data in the name column to lower case

Change data types

 df[“Passed”] = df[“Passed”].astype(bool)

Remove duplicate values

df = df.drop_duplicates()
